description:
Fix rename_tab API bug and implement proper name tracking.

**Bug**: rename_tab() needs the tab ID, but TabInfo doesn't expose it directly.

**Solution**: Parse tab ID from default name pattern 'Tab #N':
```rust
fn parse_default_name(name: &str) -> Option<u32> {
    // "Tab #5" → Some(5) (the tab_id for rename_tab)
    if name.starts_with("Tab #") {
        name[5..].parse().ok()
    } else {
        None
    }
}

// Then call:
rename_tab(tab_id, new_name)
```

**Name tracking**: Now handled by LeaderState.tabs: HashMap<String, TabState>
- Key is tab name (stable)
- TabState includes user_defined flag
- No position tracking needed

**Note**: Only leader calls rename_tab(). Renderers never rename.

**Files**: src/main.rs
